  "term": "glia",
  "definition": "Glia are the non-neuronal cells of the nervous system. They support and protect nerve tissue, help maintain the chemical environment around neurons, contribute to barriers such as the blood-brain barrier, form myelin, assist brain development and injury responses, and exchange substances with neurons.",
